r": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.393}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "posterior": 0.574, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 3, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Constitutional symptoms with blasts provide weak evidence for lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders (B4) but do not…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B3", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=67%, source=primekg]\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  he experienced a headache with blurry vision → seizure → Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm"}
